Upstream sets ABSL_DEFAULT_LINKOPTS to "-ignore:4221" whenever
CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID is "MSVC", to silence link.exe's benign LNK4221
("no public symbols") warning. absl_cc_library() applies this to every
target's link options, including header-only INTERFACE libraries, so it
ends up baked into INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES in the exported
abslTargets.cmake and propagates to every consumer that links against
abseil.

vcpkg builds this port with real cl.exe (CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID is
"MSVC" there), but a consumer that links with clang++ using the
GNU-style driver (not clang-cl) targeting the MSVC ABI has no such
passthrough for MSVC-style dashed linker flags: it rejects
"-ignore:4221" as an unknown compiler argument, so any executable that
transitively depends on abseil fails to link.

The flag only suppresses a cosmetic warning, so drop it entirely
rather than trying to strip it back out of the generated CMake config
after the fact.

--- a/absl/copts/AbseilConfigureCopts.cmake
+++ b/absl/copts/AbseilConfigureCopts.cmake
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
 elseif(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "MSVC")
   set(ABSL_DEFAULT_COPTS "${ABSL_MSVC_FLAGS}")
   set(ABSL_TEST_COPTS "${ABSL_MSVC_TEST_FLAGS}")
-  set(ABSL_DEFAULT_LINKOPTS "${ABSL_MSVC_LINKOPTS}")
+  set(ABSL_DEFAULT_LINKOPTS "")
 else()
   message(WARNING "Unknown compiler: ${CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER}.  Building with no default flags")
   set(ABSL_DEFAULT_COPTS "")
